 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? Draw each line a few times before putting pen to paper. Then tilt the paper slightly as you draw, about ten degrees. Start with simple shapes, circles, squares and lines. Get used to drawing them exactly before putting anything on paper. Find free drawing apps on your phone. The point is doing lots of quick, messy drawings without censoring. It' meant to be awkward. The point is not to make something pretty, it's about getting your hand and eye working together.",
